      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This policy section affirms our unwavering commitment to the therapeutic right of nations to preserve their cultural heritage, recognizing that the retention of colonial artifacts often serves as a permanent reminder of oppression and inequity. We argue that repatriation is not merely a historical correction but a fundamental ethical duty to restore dignity, agency, and proper stewardship to communities that have excluded their own past for too long. By actively returning these items today, we align our museum's values with global standards of justice, fostering culturally revitalized communities while demonstrating leadership in ethical governance.",
