      "content": "We recognize the significant role major international museums play in preserving sensitive artifacts through advanced conservation technologies and world-class scholarly expertise that may currently be unavailable to their preceding nations. Moving these objects presents immediate, tangible risks, including potential damage from climate fluctuations, transportation hazards, and the loss of centuries accumulated research data lost in unfamiliar local contexts. Therefore, temporarily retaining these items in specialized global hubs serves as a stabilizing measure that guarantees their physical safety while we collaborate to build robust local infrastructure for long-term independence. *Essentially* and *ethically*, protecting the property from active harm and preserving the integrity of scientific study outweighs the abstract benefits of display control in vulnerable settings.",
